  "liner": {
   "body_md": "## What listeners single out\n\n- First time played live; Black Sabbath-inspired. Owen Pallett later picked it as the single from In League With Dragons [1]\n- Introduced by notable stage talk about the baroque inner shell of defense mechanisms [1]\n\n## Setlist highlights\n\n- **The Mountain Goats — 01 — Intro (Dusty Rhodes promo - Mid-Atlantic Wrestling, Oct. 29, 1985)**: earliest performance in the archive; legendary: the only archived performance [2]\n- **The Mountain Goats — 02 — Blood Capsules**: rare: 8 archived performances [2]\n- **The Mountain Goats — 07 — Banter - Heel Turn 2**: earliest performance in the archive; legendary: the only archived performance [2]\n- **The Mountain Goats — 09 — Banter - Store**: earliest performance in the archive; legendary: the only archived performance [2]\n- **The Mountain Goats — 10 — Store**: back after 71 archived shows (2284 days); rare: 5 archived performances [2]\n- **The Mountain Goats — 11 — Banter about remembering the lyrics to Store**: earliest performance in the archive; legendary: the only archived performance [2]\n- **The Mountain Goats — 13 — Towel situation**: earliest performance in the archive; legendary: the only archived performance [2]\n- **The Mountain Goats — 14 — Banter - Passaic, 1975**: earliest performance in the archive; legendary: the only archived performance [2]\n- Earliest performances in the archive: The Mountain Goats — 15 — Passaic, 1975 [2]\n\n## The recordings\n\n- **tmg2015-05-29** (recommended): source not stated; 36 songs; 96 min [1]\n\n## Around the show\n\n- Show was part of the Regional Heat Tour supporting Beat the Champ, at the Showbox in Seattle [1]\n\n## Tapers and lineage\n\n- **tmg2015-05-29**: taped by ∂®∑@Mßøä†; source: iPhone [1]",
